Parser Types in Compiler Design

Parser
│
├── Top-Down Parser
│     │
│     ├── Recursive Descent Parser
│     └── LL(1) Parser
│
└── Bottom-Up Parser
      │
      ├── Shift Reduce Parser
      ├── Operator Precedence Parser
      └── LR Parsers
            │
            ├── LR(0)
            ├── SLR(1)Simple LR
            ├── Canonical LR(1) CLR / Canonical LR(1)
            └── Look Ahead LR LALR(1)

Top-Down Parsing
Grammar
   ↓
Sentence

E
↓
T
↓
id

Bottom-Up Parsing
Sentence
   ↓
Grammar

id
↓
T
↓
E


What is LL
LL is a Top-Down Parsing family.

L  = Left-to-right scanning
L  = Leftmost derivation

What is LR?
LR is a Bottom-Up Parsing family.

L = Left-to-right scan

R = Rightmost derivation
    in reverse








| Feature           | LL(1)            | LR(1)          |
| ----------------- | ---------------- | -------------- |
| Type              | Top Down         | Bottom Up      |
| Parse Tree        | Root → Leaves    | Leaves → Root  |
| Left Recursion    | Not Allowed      | Allowed        |
| Easy to Implement | Yes              | Hard           |
| Power             | Less             | More           |
| Speed             | Fast             | Fast           |
| Used in           | Simple Languages | Real Compilers |






